4993	736	13	The fever, which invades the principle of lymph chyle, blood, flesh or fat, is easily curable, while the one, which affects the bone or marrow, and is detected from the atrophy and discolouring of the locality affected, can be made amenable to medicine only with the greatest difficulty. This type of fever is further characterised by unconscious or sub-comatose of tire patient, hyperpyrexia, frequent loose motions of warm muco-billious matter, and an angry look of the eyes.
