5318	789	11	A cosmetic composed of Lodhra, Kumkum, Manjistha, Loha, Kaleyakam, barley, rice, and Yasthimadhu pasted together with water should be used by ladies for beautifying their complexion. Cook a Prastha measure of oil with two parts of goat’s milk and a Karsha of each of the following drugs, viz., Rakta-Chandanam, Manjishtha, Laksha, Yashtimadhu, and Kumkum. This Tailam is highly possessed of cosmetic properties; a week’s application will impart a beautiful tint to one’s complexion.
5319	789	12	A decoction of Shunthi, powdered Pippali, Guduchi, and Kantakarika, acts as a good digestant and stomachic remedy, and tends to alleviate, O Thou, the lord of benighted spirits, the aching (rheumatic) pain brought about through the agency of the deranged Vayu.
