5322	789	15	Milk cooked with Shunthi acts as a good febrifuge. Errhines composed of Yashthimadhu, Musta, Vrihatiphalam and rock salt pounded together is possessed of highly soporific properties. Similarly, errhines composed of Maricha pasted with honey, O Shiva, are possessed of the virtue of inducing sleep. O Shiva, Kakajangha roots are possessed of good soporific properties, and a medicinal oil cooked in combination with Kanjikam and Sarja-rasa, applied with the admixture of cold water, instantly allays heat and burning sensation, and should be employed in alleviating the burning sensation of the body which characterises fever of contaminated blood (fever induced through blood-poisoning or Septecimia).
